## Find an example by capability

- **LAA starters:** [laa-data-claims-api](https://github.com/ministryofjustice/laa-data-claims-api)
  combines the auth, export, and SQL scanner starters;
  [laa-provider-data-platform](https://github.com/ministryofjustice/laa-provider-data-platform)
  combines auth and OAuth2.
- **MapStruct:** [laa-data-access-api](https://github.com/ministryofjustice/laa-data-access-api)
  and [laa-provider-data-platform](https://github.com/ministryofjustice/laa-provider-data-platform)
  show mapping alongside persistence and API boundaries.
- **Oracle and JPA:** [laa-ccms-caab-api](https://github.com/ministryofjustice/laa-ccms-caab-api)
  and [laa-data-provider-data](https://github.com/ministryofjustice/laa-data-provider-data)
  provide examples shaped by legacy integration constraints.
- **PostgreSQL, Flyway, and JPA:**
  [laa-data-access-api](https://github.com/ministryofjustice/laa-data-access-api),
  [laa-data-claims-api](https://github.com/ministryofjustice/laa-data-claims-api), and
  [laa-provider-data-platform](https://github.com/ministryofjustice/laa-provider-data-platform)
  show the three technologies together.
- **Templates and shared tooling:**
  [laa-spring-boot-common](https://github.com/ministryofjustice/laa-spring-boot-common),
  [laa-spring-boot-microservice-template](https://github.com/ministryofjustice/laa-spring-boot-microservice-template),
  and [laa-spring-boot-ui-template](https://github.com/ministryofjustice/laa-spring-boot-ui-template)
  show supported defaults and reusable build components.

The catalogue is a point-in-time learning aid. Confirm a repository's current implementation before
adopting its approach.
